# Cloudflare Pages routing. The app is a History-API SPA: every view has a real
# path (/privacy, /play/{code}, /profile/collection), and none of those paths is
# a file on disk. Without this line Pages 404s all of them — a refresh, a
# bookmark, a shared session link, and the two legal URLs Google's brand review
# has to load.
#
# vercel.json's "rewrites" block does the same job on Vercel and Pages does NOT
# read it, so the rule has to exist twice while both hosts are live. Keep them
# in step; deleting vercel.json is part of the Vercel teardown, not before.
#
# 200, not 301/302: the browser must keep the URL it asked for so the router can
# resolve it. A redirect would rewrite the address bar to / and lose the route.
# Pages serves a real static asset first and only falls through to this, so the
# bundle, assets/ and config.js are unaffected.
/*  /index.html  200
